Retry a main-frame load that fails

When the main frame's load fails, for any reason but being superseded by
another load, load the launch argument again 5 s later, and again after
every failure until a load succeeds. WebKit's error page stays up
meanwhile. A browser that starts before its backend listens, or whose
reload lands during a backend restart, is no longer left on the error page.

This is C inside surf's load handling, so it cannot be a bbappend change.

Applies after 0002-reload-a-page-that-stops-answering.patch.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [kiosk-specific]
